When was the last time you misplaced your keys, glasses, or cell phone? Or ran into an acquaintance and couldn't come up with their name no matter how hard you racked your brain? Have you ever gotten into an argument with a sibling over whether a childhood memory really happened the way you thought it did? Both of you sure that your memory was correct? Human memory is imperfect. For most people, it's easy to think of examples of these common but frustrating situations.
