00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:58.000
that they just haven't really thought about for a while. And that's not an unusual occurrence. Memory of a past event that I haven't thought about for a while may be triggered by a queue. And that seems to kind of fit a lot of the recovered memory experiences that people report that can be corroborated, those spontaneous reminders. And it's not necessarily the case that those memories were actively repressed. it's just something people hadn't thought about for a while, and then it can be reminded of later. On the other side of that, there's also, you know, there was even by 2001 a lot of evidence that many of
他们只是有一段时间没有真正想过。这并不是一种不寻常的发生。我有一段时间没有想过的过去事件的记忆可能会被线索触发。这似乎在某种程度上符合人们报告的、可以被证实的许多恢复的记忆体验，那些自发的提醒。而且这些记忆不一定是被主动压抑的；这只是人们有一段时间没有想过的事情，然后以后可以被提醒。在另一方面，还有，你知道，即使到2001年也有很多证据表明许多

