我认为这在几个不同的方面都很重要。从经验上讲，这种联系在于，当我们回忆过去的经历时，我们所参与的许多过程，与我们展望未来并想象可能发生的经历时所参与的过程是相同的。例如，在我的实验室里，我们大约在15年前开始系统地进行这项工作，让人们进入扫描仪，给他们简单的词汇提示，并要求他们要么回忆过去的经历，要么想象与该词汇提示相关的未来经历。例如，对于“度假”这个词，如果你处于记忆条件下，你会尝试检索过去几年中关于度假的具体记忆。在未来条件下，如果你得到同样的词汇提示，你会想象未来几年内可能发生的度假。我们比较了大脑活动。

47
00:33:42.000 --> 00:34:32.000
in those two conditions to a control condition where you'd be given the same kinds of cues and asked to perform tasks that involve both visual and conceptual processing, but didn't involve remembering or imagining a specific event. And what we saw was very striking increases in a network of brain regions during remembering the past and imagining the future that were nearly, not entirely, but nearly identical, suggesting a strong link between. between the two. And indeed, that work was in part stimulated by an interesting observation from the 1980s that was made by Endel Tollving, an eminent memory researcher, my old PhD advisor and colleague at the University of Toronto when I was there back in the 70s and 80s. And this
