00:36:44.000 --> 00:37:36.000
for reminiscing about the past, but for using past experience to plan ahead to simulate future events, which is kind of the way I look at it, memory is useful to the extent that it can help us predict, anticipate, simulate the future. For a memory system to be helpful as a guide to future thinking, we need it to be a flexible system. we need to be able to recombine bits and pieces of our past experience to simulate novel upcoming events, because after all, the future is rarely identical to the past. So one of my arguments over the past 15 years has been that one of the reasons why we have memory errors, certain memory misattributions, where we mix up elements of different events,
